+## Filtering
+
+The list can be narrowed by name and by status. Both are applied by the
+repository, before paging and counting, so the grid stays lazy however many
+customers match; the line above the grid reports the backend's count, not the
+number of rows loaded.
+
+The filter lives in the URL, as `?name=vir&status=ACTIVE,CLOSED`, so a narrowed
+list can be bookmarked or sent to a colleague. Typing waits for a pause before
+it reaches the backend, and updates the address bar in place rather than adding
+a history entry per keystroke.
+
 The 500 customers live in `src/main/resources/customers.csv` and are loaded once
 at startup.

